  "script": "An AI built a playable 3D shooter in one HTML file. It’s called Saltline. Anthropic engineer Felix Rieseberg used Claude Fable 5.2. One initial prompt. No human feedback during the run. Eight hours later: a playable FPS. Set in a rainy industrial harbor. The file size? About 1.4 megabytes. No image files. No audio files. No 3D model downloads. Code generates geometry, textures, and sound. The reported run: 2.7 million output tokens. Roughly five hundred fifty dollars in API cost. Not a AAA game. But a wild proof of what AI can build.",
